From e0af579a16d58b594fcb980a593a4c338d77b7db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 15:01:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03098/11362] [outer-loop] steer .417 A3/A4/A6/B2 with the
 solve-rate-preserving lever contract

The conductor's queued .417 levers would fail the SAME knife-edge way A1/A2 did
unless they are solve-rate-preserving BY CONSTRUCTION. Injected the contract
into the (not-yet-run) task prompts (outer-loop edits YAML only; conductor
implements the explorer code -- zero file race):

- A3 (adaptive budget): DEFER not DELETE -- move the top candidate to the FRONT
  of node['untested'] and KEEP the tail; never return [rows[0]] (the destructive
  filter that reproduces the A1/A2 knife-edge). Commit only on re-visited frames.
  Report committed_frame_fraction_on_winning_path (if ~0 the lever is inert).
- A4 (lazy best-first): keep depth the PRIMARY sort key; lazy top-K is SCORING
  not FILTERING (dropping the tail is forbidden); DROP w=5 (the explorer's own
  comment documents a value-override regressed the baseline) -> sweep {0,0.5,1,2};
  a weight wins only if core_solves_preserved AND median_actions_on_core < w=0.
- A6 (integration): wire only CORE-containment-passing levers (value_weight=0 is
  an acceptable honest null); diagnose the real 97%-of-cost axis -- the
  RESET-replay nav tax -- by MEASURING forward_walk_hit_rate (the .416 nav fix
  half-engaged: _serve sets awaiting but _ingest still gates on h!=origin).
- B2: notes the CORE-containment gate is ALREADY shipped (eefd3b15a); B2
  canonicalizes + CI-guards the four fixtures + measures the headroom budget B*
  (no blind cap raise).

All driven by the CORE set-containment gate (eefd3b15a). YAML re-validated: 12
tasks intact, parses clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
