+      1. SOLVE-RATE-PRESERVING LEVER CONTRACT (outer-loop 2026-06-20, MANDATORY): keep `depth` the PRIMARY sort key in _frontier -- use the existing blend (depth + w*value, depth, -on_path); value_weight=0 is the provable no-regression CONTROL. The lazy top-K eval (exp4506) decides only WHICH candidates get the EXPENSIVE value score -- the tail keeps its CHEAP priority and REMAINS expandable. Wiring top-K as a FILTER (dropping the tail) is FORBIDDEN: it re-introduces the A1/A2 knife-edge failure. best_first reorders node expansion but still explores the whole reachable set, so it is solve-rate-preserving by construction. Wire best_first over the value head with the LAZY eval (top-K / frame-hash cache from exp4506).
+      2. Sweep value_weight in {0.0, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0} -- DROP w=5 (the explorer's own comment at arc_competition_agent.py ~line 495 documents a value-override regressed the baseline; do not re-run the known regression). Per weight report (held-out solve-rate, median_actions_on_core, median per-game wall-seconds).
       3. value_weight=0 is the explicit CONTROL (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK).
-      4. If a weight>0 beats 0 on solve-rate AND stays within the ~6.5 min/game budget AND does not raise median actions -> raise SUBMITTED_VALUE_WEIGHT + update test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py consistently. Else keep 0 + honest null.
+      4. GATE = CORE set-containment over {lp85,m0r0,sp80,vc33} (scripts/kaggle/arc_local_submission_gate.py already implements it). A weight WINS only if core_solves_preserved AND median_actions_on_core < the w=0 control AND median per-game wall-time stays in the ~6.5 min/game budget -> raise SUBMITTED_VALUE_WEIGHT + update test_arc_submitted_agent_parity.py consistently. Else keep 0 + honest null. A weight that wins on actions but blows wall-time is NOT submittable.
       5. Solves stay offline-reproduced via arc_solver_kit.reproduce.
 
